+msgstr "Un math:ApproximateValue qui nomme une cible exacte égale à un tiers au moyen de math:approximates mais omet math:approximationError illustre le cas d’une borne manquante. Lire le composant et la forme source du constat avant d’identifier ce cas dans un rapport."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExactApproximateConflation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use when interpreting findings attributed to the canonical math:ApproximateValue restrictions on its exact target and the presence of a numeric error bound."
+msgstr "À utiliser pour interpréter les constats attribués aux restrictions canoniques de math:ApproximateValue concernant sa cible exacte et la présence d’une borne numérique d’erreur."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExactApproximateConflation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Avoid treating this class as proof of an incorrect numerical value, a negative bound, mismatched literal and declared datatypes, or equality between the approximation and target resources; the current restriction group establishes none of those numerical or identity judgments."
+msgstr "Ne pas considérer cette classe comme une preuve d’une valeur numérique incorrecte, d’une borne négative, d’un désaccord entre le type du littéral et le type déclaré, ou d’une identité entre les ressources de l’approximation et de sa cible ; le groupe actuel de restrictions n’établit aucun de ces jugements numériques ou d’identité."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExactApproximateConflation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Inspect the component, path, value and source shape, then repair the reported obligation: retain a separate math:ApproximateValue, one justified math:Number target through math:approximates and a numeric absolute math:approximationError bound. Validation derives from the existing logic restrictions; establish the bound's numerical justification separately."
+msgstr "Examiner le composant, le chemin, la valeur et la forme source, puis corriger l’obligation signalée : conserver un math:ApproximateValue distinct, une seule cible math:Number justifiée au moyen de math:approximates et une borne numérique absolue math:approximationError. La validation dérive des restrictions logic existantes ; établir séparément la justification numérique de la borne."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ConstantAsDecimalLiteral|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Constant as Decimal Literal"
+msgstr "Constante exprimée par un littéral décimal"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ConstantAsDecimalLiteral|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "The failure raised when a math:MathematicalConstant is given as a decimal literal — it carries a raw math:quantityValue directly instead of being an exact individual. A constant's decimal expansion belongs to a distinct math:ApproximateValue that math:approximates it."
+msgstr "La défaillance signalée lorsqu’un math:MathematicalConstant est donné sous forme de littéral décimal : il porte directement une valeur brute math:quantityValue au lieu d’être un individu exact. Le développement décimal d’une constante appartient à un math:ApproximateValue distinct qui la désigne au moyen de math:approximates."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ConstantAsDecimalLiteral|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "The named constant keeps its exact identity independently of any numerical representation. The current math:MathematicalConstant-level report annotation also covers its isExact obligations, so this class alone does not establish that a quantityValue literal was present."
+msgstr "La constante nommée conserve son identité exacte indépendamment de toute représentation numérique. L’annotation actuelle des rapports au niveau de math:MathematicalConstant couvre également ses obligations isExact ; cette classe seule n’établit donc pas qu’un littéral quantityValue était présent."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ConstantAsDecimalLiteral|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "A math:MathematicalConstant with math:isExact true and a direct math:quantityValue of 3.14159 typed as xsd:double illustrates the forbidden-literal case. A justified numerical evaluation belongs on a separate math:ApproximateValue that math:approximates the constant."
+msgstr "Un math:MathematicalConstant portant math:isExact true et directement une math:quantityValue de 3.14159 de type xsd:double illustre le cas du littéral interdit. Une évaluation numérique justifiée appartient à un math:ApproximateValue distinct qui désigne la constante au moyen de math:approximates."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ConstantAsDecimalLiteral|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use when interpreting findings associated with the existing constant-local exactness or absence-of-direct-literal obligations while preserving the exact named individual."
+msgstr "À utiliser pour interpréter les constats associés aux obligations existantes d’exactitude ou d’absence de littéral direct propres aux constantes, tout en préservant l’individu nommé exact."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ConstantAsDecimalLiteral|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Avoid changing the constant's exact identity because an evaluation is rounded, limiting the literal prohibition to xsd:decimal because of this class's label, or inferring a particular violation component from the class alone."
+msgstr "Ne pas modifier l’identité exacte de la constante parce qu’une évaluation est arrondie, limiter l’interdiction des littéraux à xsd:decimal à cause du libellé de cette classe, ou déduire un composant particulier de violation de la seule classe."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ConstantAsDecimalLiteral|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Read the reported component, path, value and source shape. Remove a direct math:quantityValue literal from the constant when present, retain math:isExact true, and keep any justified evaluation and numeric absolute error bound on a separate math:ApproximateValue. Repair the actual reported obligation without replacing the canonical constant identity."
+msgstr "Lire le composant, le chemin, la valeur et la forme source signalés. Retirer de la constante tout littéral direct math:quantityValue présent, conserver math:isExact true et placer toute évaluation justifiée et sa borne numérique absolue d’erreur sur un math:ApproximateValue distinct. Corriger l’obligation effectivement signalée sans remplacer l’identité canonique de la constante."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathConformanceFailure|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Math Conformance Failure"
+msgstr "Défaut de conformité mathématique"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathConformanceFailure|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "The class of situations in which a mathematical well-formedness or preservation obligation is violated. Its subclasses identify kinds of failure that validation findings can report."
+msgstr "La classe des situations où une obligation de bonne formation ou de préservation mathématique est violée. Ses sous-classes identifient les types de défaillance que les constats de validation peuvent signaler."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathConformanceFailure|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "Canonical logic axioms and constraints state the applicable obligations. A class IRI on a finding identifies the kind of situation observed. One class can cover several checks."
+msgstr "Les axiomes et les contraintes de la logique canonique énoncent les obligations applicables. L’IRI de classe d’un constat identifie le type de situation observée. Une même classe peut couvrir plusieurs contrôles."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathConformanceFailure|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "A finding attributed to math:UnsituatedNumber identifies a number-system validation problem. Its path and constraint component show which part of the obligation failed."
+msgstr "Un constat attribué à math:UnsituatedNumber signale un problème de validation du système de nombres. Son chemin et son composant de contrainte indiquent quelle partie de l’obligation est violée."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathConformanceFailure|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use as a parent for a class that identifies a kind of violation of an authored mathematical obligation."
+msgstr "Utiliser comme classe parente d’une classe qui identifie un type de violation d’une obligation mathématique définie dans la source."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathConformanceFailure|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Use the finding record for validation details. Establish numerical or empirical claims with evidence appropriate to those claims."
+msgstr "Consulter le constat pour les détails de validation. Étayer les affirmations numériques ou empiriques par des éléments de preuve adaptés."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathConformanceFailure|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Choose the most specific failure class supported by the check. Keep the class IRI and the focus node, path, component, value and source shape when the finding provides them."
+msgstr "Choisir la classe de défaillance la plus précise établie par le contrôle. Conserver l’IRI de classe, ainsi que le nœud ciblé, le chemin, le composant, la valeur et la forme source lorsque le constat les fournit."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnsituatedNumber|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Unsituated Number"
+msgstr "Nombre sans système déclaré"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnsituatedNumber|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "A failure of the requirement for a math:Number to declare exactly one math:NumberSystem through math:inNumberSystem."
+msgstr "Un manquement à l’obligation pour un math:Number de déclarer exactement un math:NumberSystem par math:inNumberSystem."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnsituatedNumber|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "The obligation on math:Number covers both the type of the system and the number of values. Admissible targets include the ordinary named system individuals and math:ExtendedRealLine. The mathematical context determines whether the chosen system describes the number."
+msgstr "L’obligation applicable à math:Number porte sur le type du système et sur le nombre de valeurs. Les cibles admissibles comprennent les individus des systèmes usuels nommés et math:ExtendedRealLine. Le contexte mathématique permet de déterminer si le système choisi décrit le nombre."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnsituatedNumber|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "A math:RationalNumber marked math:isExact true with no math:inNumberSystem link illustrates a missing-system case. A valid declaration for the exact number one third links to math:rationalNumbers."
+msgstr "Un math:RationalNumber marqué math:isExact true et dépourvu de lien math:inNumberSystem illustre le cas d’un système manquant. Une déclaration valide du nombre exact un tiers pointe vers math:rationalNumbers."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnsituatedNumber|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use to interpret a finding attributed to the math:inNumberSystem requirement on math:Number."
+msgstr "Utiliser pour interpréter un constat attribué à l’obligation math:inNumberSystem sur math:Number."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnsituatedNumber|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Use the reported component to investigate whether a system link is missing. Assess exactness and mathematical membership independently."
+msgstr "Examiner le composant signalé pour déterminer si un lien vers un système manque. Évaluer séparément l’exactitude et l’appartenance mathématique."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/UnsituatedNumber|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Read the focus node, component, path, value and source shape for the reported problem. Repair the declaration so math:inNumberSystem points to one justified math:NumberSystem individual. Express containment between systems through math:subsystemOf."
+msgstr "Lire le nœud ciblé, le composant, le chemin, la valeur et la forme source associés au problème signalé. Corriger la déclaration pour que math:inNumberSystem pointe vers un seul individu math:NumberSystem dont le choix est justifié. Exprimer l’inclusion entre systèmes par math:subsystemOf."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/math/tests/ecNumberSituated|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/conformanceRationale"
+msgid "The control declares a math:RationalNumber with math:isExact true and exactly one math:inNumberSystem value, math:rationalNumbers. The cell expects a conforming result from the generated validation surface."
+msgstr "Le témoin déclare un math:RationalNumber avec math:isExact true et exactement une valeur de math:inNumberSystem, à savoir math:rationalNumbers. Le résultat attendu de la validation générée est la conformité."
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/math/tests/ecNumberMissingSystem|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/conformanceRationale"
+msgid "The counter-example declares exactness but omits math:inNumberSystem. Class isolation requires at least one math:UnsituatedNumber finding and rejects findings outside that class in the selected channels."
+msgstr "Le contre-exemple déclare l’exactitude et omet math:inNumberSystem. La vérification de l’isolation de la classe exige au moins un constat math:UnsituatedNumber et rejette les constats associés à d’autres classes dans les canaux sélectionnés."
diff --git slices/grounding/math/i18n/zh.po slices/grounding/math/i18n/zh.po
index 676b578be..9e8956575 100644
--- slices/grounding/math/i18n/zh.po
+++ slices/grounding/math/i18n/zh.po
@@ -3674,8 +3674,8 @@ msgid "Number"
 msgstr "数"
 
 msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Number|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
-msgid "A mathematical number: an abstract quantity that lives in a declared number system. Every math:Number situates itself in a math:NumberSystem through math:inNumberSystem — an unsituated number is ill-formed — and declares through math:isExact whether it is an exact value or the abstract counterpart that a math:ApproximateValue approximates. The five nested systems ℕ ⊂ ℤ ⊂ ℚ ⊂ ℝ ⊂ ℂ are its principal subclasses."
-msgstr "数学中的数：属于一个已声明数系的抽象量。每个 math:Number 都通过 math:inNumberSystem 将自身置于一个 math:NumberSystem 中；未指定数系的数不合规范。它还通过 math:isExact 声明自身是精确值，还是某个 math:ApproximateValue 所近似的抽象对应对象。五个嵌套数系 ℕ ⊂ ℤ ⊂ ℚ ⊂ ℝ ⊂ ℂ 对应其主要子类。"
+msgid "An abstract mathematical number with an identity in the graph. A number has one declared math:NumberSystem through math:inNumberSystem. Classes such as math:RationalNumber refine its classification, while named systems such as math:rationalNumbers are values of that property. Record exactness with math:isExact independently of any math:ApproximateValue that names the number as its target."
+msgstr "在图中具有明确身份的抽象数。每个数通过 math:inNumberSystem 声明一个 math:NumberSystem。math:RationalNumber 等类细化数的分类，math:rationalNumbers 等命名数系是该属性的值。用 math:isExact 记录精确性，这独立于是否有 math:ApproximateValue 将该数作为目标。"
 
 msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/Number|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
 msgid "This class describes mathematical objects, not RDF numeric literals or the sets that contain numbers. Select a more specific number class when known; math:inNumberSystem names a system individual rather than a class."
@@ -18390,3 +18390,123 @@ msgstr "避免零值、分母缺失、非整数字面量，或对规范 RDF 推
 msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/denominator|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
 msgid "Supply one nonzero xsd:integer value with the carrier's math:numerator. Check the class-local datatype/count/closure obligations and the explicit forbidden-zero constraint. Preserve full diagnostic evidence when generated validation reports a violation."
 msgstr "为载体提供一个非零的 xsd:integer 值，并同时提供其 math:numerator。检查类局部的数据类型、计数和闭合义务，以及显式禁止零值的约束。当生成的验证报告指出约束违反时，应保留完整的诊断证据。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExactApproximateConflation|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Exact–Approximate Conflation"
+msgstr "精确值与近似值混淆"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExactApproximateConflation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "The failure raised when a math:ApproximateValue fails to keep an approximation distinct from the exact value — it does not name, through math:approximates, the exact number it stands in for, or does not declare its math:approximationError. An exact number and an approximation of it are distinct objects."
+msgstr "当 math:ApproximateValue 未将近似值与精确值区分开时报告的失败：它未通过 math:approximates 指明所代表的精确数，或未声明 math:approximationError。精确数与该数的近似值是不同的对象。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExactApproximateConflation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "This class describes a failure of approximation framing. Its current math:ApproximateValue-level report annotation can also classify target-type or count findings; the class alone proves neither resource-identity conflation nor the validity of a numerical error bound."
+msgstr "该类描述近似值描述框架的缺陷。当前位于 math:ApproximateValue 类级别的报告注释也可用于归类目标类型或值数量方面的发现；仅凭该类既不能证明两个资源被视为同一对象，也不能证明数值误差界有效。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExactApproximateConflation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "A math:ApproximateValue that names an exact one-third target through math:approximates but omits math:approximationError illustrates the missing-bound case. Read the finding's component and source shape before identifying that case from a report."
+msgstr "一个 math:ApproximateValue 通过 math:approximates 指明精确的三分之一目标，却省略 math:approximationError，展示了缺少误差界的情形。在根据报告认定这一情形前，应读取发现的约束组件和来源形状。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExactApproximateConflation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use when interpreting findings attributed to the canonical math:ApproximateValue restrictions on its exact target and the presence of a numeric error bound."
+msgstr "用于解释归属于 math:ApproximateValue 规范约束的发现，这些约束涉及其精确目标及数值误差界是否存在。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExactApproximateConflation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Avoid treating this class as proof of an incorrect numerical value, a negative bound, mismatched literal and declared datatypes, or equality between the approximation and target resources; the current restriction group establishes none of those numerical or identity judgments."
+msgstr "不要将该类视为数值错误、误差界为负、字面量类型与声明类型不符，或近似值资源与目标资源相同的证明；当前约束组并不确立这些数值或身份判断。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ExactApproximateConflation|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Inspect the component, path, value and source shape, then repair the reported obligation: retain a separate math:ApproximateValue, one justified math:Number target through math:approximates and a numeric absolute math:approximationError bound. Validation derives from the existing logic restrictions; establish the bound's numerical justification separately."
+msgstr "检查约束组件、路径、值和来源形状，然后修复所报告的义务：保留独立的 math:ApproximateValue，通过 math:approximates 指向一个有依据的 math:Number 目标，并提供数值绝对误差界 math:approximationError。验证由现有 logic 约束派生；误差界的数值依据须另行建立。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ConstantAsDecimalLiteral|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Constant as Decimal Literal"
+msgstr "以十进制字面量表示常数"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ConstantAsDecimalLiteral|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "The failure raised when a math:MathematicalConstant is given as a decimal literal — it carries a raw math:quantityValue directly instead of being an exact individual. A constant's decimal expansion belongs to a distinct math:ApproximateValue that math:approximates it."
+msgstr "当 math:MathematicalConstant 被表示为十进制字面量时报告的失败：它直接携带原始 math:quantityValue，而不是保持为精确个体。常数的十进制展开属于独立的 math:ApproximateValue，该对象通过 math:approximates 指向此常数。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ConstantAsDecimalLiteral|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "The named constant keeps its exact identity independently of any numerical representation. The current math:MathematicalConstant-level report annotation also covers its isExact obligations, so this class alone does not establish that a quantityValue literal was present."
+msgstr "命名常数的精确身份独立于任何数值表示而保留。当前位于 math:MathematicalConstant 类级别的报告注释也涵盖其 isExact 义务，因此仅凭该类不能确定曾存在 quantityValue 字面量。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ConstantAsDecimalLiteral|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "A math:MathematicalConstant with math:isExact true and a direct math:quantityValue of 3.14159 typed as xsd:double illustrates the forbidden-literal case. A justified numerical evaluation belongs on a separate math:ApproximateValue that math:approximates the constant."
+msgstr "一个 math:MathematicalConstant 声明 math:isExact true，并直接携带类型为 xsd:double、数值为 3.14159 的 math:quantityValue，展示了被禁止的字面量情形。有依据的数值求值结果应放在独立的 math:ApproximateValue 上，并由该对象通过 math:approximates 指向常数。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ConstantAsDecimalLiteral|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
+msgid "Use when interpreting findings associated with the existing constant-local exactness or absence-of-direct-literal obligations while preserving the exact named individual."
+msgstr "用于解释与常数现有局部义务相关的发现，包括精确性义务和不得直接携带字面量的义务，同时保留精确的命名个体。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ConstantAsDecimalLiteral|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
+msgid "Avoid changing the constant's exact identity because an evaluation is rounded, limiting the literal prohibition to xsd:decimal because of this class's label, or inferring a particular violation component from the class alone."
+msgstr "不要因某次求值经过舍入而改变常数的精确身份，不要因该类的标签而把字面量禁令仅限于 xsd:decimal，也不要仅凭该类推断具体的违规约束组件。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/ConstantAsDecimalLiteral|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
+msgid "Read the reported component, path, value and source shape. Remove a direct math:quantityValue literal from the constant when present, retain math:isExact true, and keep any justified evaluation and numeric absolute error bound on a separate math:ApproximateValue. Repair the actual reported obligation without replacing the canonical constant identity."
+msgstr "读取所报告的约束组件、路径、值和来源形状。若常数上存在直接的 math:quantityValue 字面量，则将其移除；保留 math:isExact true，并将任何有依据的求值结果及数值绝对误差界放在独立的 math:ApproximateValue 上。修复实际报告的义务，不要替换常数的规范身份。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathConformanceFailure|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
+msgid "Math Conformance Failure"
+msgstr "数学规范违例"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathConformanceFailure|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
+msgid "The class of situations in which a mathematical well-formedness or preservation obligation is violated. Its subclasses identify kinds of failure that validation findings can report."
+msgstr "数学良构义务或保持性义务遭到违反的情形所属的类。其子类指明验证发现可以报告的失败类型。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathConformanceFailure|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
+msgid "Canonical logic axioms and constraints state the applicable obligations. A class IRI on a finding identifies the kind of situation observed. One class can cover several checks."
+msgstr "规范逻辑公理和约束规定适用的义务。验证发现中的类 IRI 指明观察到的情形属于哪一类。同一个类可以涵盖多项检查。"
+
+msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/MathConformanceFailure|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
+msgid "A finding attributed to math:UnsituatedNumber identifies a number-system validation problem. Its path and constraint component show which part of the obligation failed."
